      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T20:40:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Derek, I thought you said over VC that `kNever` needs to be a negative number, but I don\u0027t remember why. If it was `MAX_INT`, can\u0027t this function just be\n\n```\nif (apiLevel \u003e\u003d fStrictVersion) return RunMode::kRunStrict;\nif (apiLevel \u003e\u003d fWorkaroundsVersion) return RunMode::kRunWithWorkarounds;\nreturn RunMode::kSkip;\n```\n\n? If `fStrictVersion` is `MAX_INT`, `apiLevel` will never be greater. Where do we rely on `kNever` being smaller than something else?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "b79e1ae5a20a0e11eaabdc1e20fdf4e979ee043d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "000a9d7b_41d934c2",
        "filename": "tests/CtsEnforcement.cpp",
